//! Girih star-and-cross tiling — the genuinely quasiperiodic girih
//! pattern generated by the **Darb-i Imam substitution system**
//! (Lu & Steinhardt, *Science* 315, 1106 (2007)), the 3-prototile
//! self-similar girih system of the Darb-i Imam shrine in Isfahan.
//!
//! # The substitution system
//!
//! Three girih prototiles with unit edges, all angles multiples of 36°:
//! * **DEC** — regular decagon (`tabl`), circumradius φ = (1+√5)/2;
//! * **HEX** — elongated hexagon / bobbin (`shesh-band`);
//! * **BOW** — bow-tie hexagon (`sormeh-dan`).
//!
//! Each tile is replaced by a fixed cluster of unit child tiles placed in
//! the parent's frame scaled by the inflation factor
//!
//! ```text
//! IF = 2·(2+√5) = 2φ³ ≈ 8.472135955
//! ```
//!
//! (20 rotation orientations, in units of 18°).  The child clusters
//! **protrude across the parent boundary**; the protruding parts of
//! adjacent replacements are *identical tiles*, which meshes the clusters
//! exactly.  The seams between adjacent clusters are filled by the
//! **edge rule**: every tile also emits *edge markers* — one for each
//! interior edge of its closed cluster (real children + the trios
//! straddling the parent's own boundary edges) — and each marker is
//! substituted by the trio `[HEX, DEC, HEX]` straddling that edge at
//! offsets ∓(3φ+1)/2 along it.  The whole bookkeeping is exact: the
//! markers of a generation are precisely the undirected edge set of that
//! generation's patch (verified exactly at generation 2, 55 080 = 55 080,
//! no duplicates), which is what makes the recursion well-defined.
//!
//! Substituting a single unit decagon at the origin (plus its 10 boundary
//! edges) and iterating produces patches with exact 10-fold rotational
//! symmetry around the seed: the classical **girih star-and-cross
//! rosette** at the centre, quasiperiodic order throughout, growing
//! outward every generation.  The arrangement is a limit tiling: within
//! the frozen core the tile set no longer changes under further
//! substitution (verified: P₂ = P₃ up to radius 79, P₃ = P₄ up to ≈ 643).
//!
//! # Exactness
//!
//! All positions live in the number field K = Q(a), a = 2cos(π/10)
//! (degree 4, basis (1, a, a², a³)); elements are stored as integer
//! 4-tuples at a global denominator of 64, in which every quantity that
//! occurs (coordinates, rotation entries, table offsets, cross/dot
//! products of them) is exact.  The tables below were derived in a Python
//! prototype by BFS-propagating child centres through exact edge-contact
//! equations and cross-checking every centre against Greg Egan's
//! reference implementation (www.gregegan.net/APPLETS/32/32.html) to
//! ≤ 1.1e-14; the marker tables were verified to be *exactly* the
//! interior-edge sets of the closed clusters.  The Rust structural tests
//! re-verify generations 1 and 2 end to end in exact arithmetic:
//! unit edges, no duplicate tiles, every interior edge matched by
//! opposite orientations, zero T-junctions, legal vertex fans,
//! Euler characteristic 2, 10-fold symmetry.
//!
//! # Generation for a view
//!
//! A single global lineage grows from the seed decagon at the origin and
//! covers a disk of radius ≈ 111.3 at depth 2, growing ×8.18 per
//! generation (the covered growth is structural: each parent's closed
//! cluster covers the parent exactly, so depth *k*+1 covers IF·depth-*k*
//! up to rim detail).  `generate` picks the smallest depth whose
//! conservative covered-radius table reaches the view's farthest corner,
//! builds the patch top-down with an S-box window cascade (each level
//! keeps only objects whose children can reach the view; child offsets
//! are bounded by 13.31 in child units, so an inter-level margin of
//! 13.31/IF ≈ 1.571 suffices — 1.6 is used), and **accepts the view only
//! when the patch covers it exactly** (clipped-area equality); otherwise
//! the depth escalates, up to [`MAX_DEPTH`] = 12 (covered radius
//! ≈ 1.2e11).  Tile emission is unit-edge at every depth; zooming in
//! deepens the patch, and inside the frozen core the tiles are
//! depth-independent.

